{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310718,"nonce":"0QWTag31HpYfdV/r2abgQ7eMUsE=","title":"FIXED 96b992fb: a loop temporary was always released as a plain allocation, so a string header went to libc free and aborted. The iteration ...","message":"**FOUND 2026-08-18 at `fee2598c`. PRE-EXISTING — reproduces with `884dfaf9`\nreverted, so it is not from this session's compiler work.**\n\n**THE REPRO — the concat result is never even used:**\n\n    class Main { static function main() { for (i in 0...5) { var s = \"i=\" + i; } Sys.println(\"done\"); } }\n\n→ **exit 134 (SIGABRT)**, nothing printed. `rayzor run Main.hx --release --llvm`.\n\n**WHAT IT IS, from the macOS crash report** (`~/Library/Logs/DiagnosticReports/rayzor-*.ips`):\n\n    ___BUG_IN_CLIENT_OF_LIBMALLOC_POINTER_BEING_FREED_WAS_NOT_ALLOCATED\n    \u003cJIT frame\u003e  -\u003e  rayzor::run_file\n\nAn invalid/double free issued BY JIT-COMPILED CODE. libmalloc's message does NOT\nreach our stderr, and none of the runtime's own abort sites fire (no\n`[array-guard]`, no `[heap-check]`, no use-after-move trap) — **so the crash is\ncompletely silent; only the .ips crash report names it.** Remember that: exit 134\nwith no output means read the DiagnosticReports file.\n\n**MATRIX (all in a loop body, `--release --llvm`):**\n\n| statement | exit |\n|---|---|\n| `var s = \"i=\" + i;` (result unused) | **134** |\n| `eat(\"i=\" + i)` into a user function | **134** |\n| `Sys.println(\"i=\" + i)` / `Sys.print(...)` | **134** |\n| `Sys.println(a + a)`, `a:String` | **134** |\n| `Sys.println(\"plain\")` — no concat | 0 |\n| `Sys.println(fmt(x))` — String from a call, no concat | 0 |\n| **`trace(\"i=\" + i)`** — identical concat | **0** |\n\nSo the trigger is the CONCAT TEMPORARY in a loop body, not `Sys.println`, and not\nthe loop form (`for` and `while` both). `trace()` masks it entirely.\n\n**WHY 184/184 TESTS STILL PASS:** the suite overwhelmingly uses `trace()`, which\ndoes not trip it — e.g. `compiler/tests/haxe/debug_while.hx` concatenates inside\ntwo loops and passes. Sys.println + concat in a loop is simply not covered. **The\nsuite is NOT evidence this path works.**\n\n**IT IS THE ROOT CAUSE OF [[bugs_bench_eval_aborts_on_second_chunk]].** That\nharness dies entering chunk 2 solely because its per-chunk line is\n`Sys.println(\"[chunk \" + chunks + \"] pos=\" + pos + ...)`. Neutering that one\nstatement makes all 3 chunks run and exit 0; restoring the scoring loop with it\nneutered also passes. So the perplexity gate is blocked by THIS bug, not by\nanything in the eval logic.\n\n**WHERE TO LOOK:** `compiler/src/ir/insert_free.rs`. Per\n[[reference_insert_free_actual_conditions]] loop-body NON-string/array allocs are\nexplicitly SKIPPED — i.e. strings in a loop body ARE dropped, which is exactly\nthis path. Suspect two drops for one temporary (a last-use drop plus a\nscope-exit drop). `255f9638` fixed the neighbouring case where a last use INSIDE\nA LOOP was freed at that statement because `should_drop_at_statement` ignored the\n`in_loop` flag — same family, and worth re-reading before touching it.\n\n**METHOD NOTE — two of my instruments lied before this landed.** Print-based\nlocalisation was TRUNCATED by stdout block-buffering (SIGABRT never flushes), and\n`RAYZOR_DISABLE_PASSES` is BUNDLE-only so a null result from it proves nothing.\n`File.saveContent` per marker is unbuffered and trustworthy; `Sys.stderr()`\nSIGILLs (unmapped extern, same family as [[bugs_map_keys_traps_exit_133]]).\n\n\n**FIXED 2026-08-18 in `96b992fb`.** `compiler/src/ir/insert_free.rs`: the\nper-iteration release path (`find_iteration_temporaries` → push at the latch)\nemitted a bare `IrInstruction::Free` for EVERY value, while the return path\nclassifies first — string ⇒ call `haxe_string_free`, array ⇒ `haxe_array_free`\nthen `Free` on the header, anon ⇒ its drop, else ⇒ bare `Free`. The file's own\ncomment already stated the rule (\"string allocs get ONLY this call, never an\n`IrInstruction::Free`\"); only the iteration path violated it. A string header is\n`Box::into_raw`, so libc `free` rejects it and libmalloc aborts — and the byte\nbuffer leaked too, because only `haxe_string_free` releases it.\n\nFix = apply the same classification at the latch. Verified: all 7 repro shapes\n(concat with Int, `a + a`, `substr`, `Sys.print`/`println`, `for` and `while`)\nnow exit 0; array and `trace` paths unchanged; **184/184 haxe tests**; clippy\nclean; llama-chat 0.5B 85 tok/s with no traps.\n\n**IT DID NOT FULLY FIX bench/eval** — see\n[[bugs_bench_eval_aborts_on_second_chunk]]. That harness now dies with exit 133\ninstead of 134, still entering chunk 2, and the crash report names\n`_xzm_xzone_malloc_freelist_outlined` — a CORRUPTED FREELIST detected at a later\nmalloc, which is a SECOND, independent corruption (same signature as the\nalready-fixed `139c4f5`). Do not assume this fix covers it.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_string_concat_in_loop_double_free` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}